WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.272
Hannah: Our acceptance criteria include identical approved reports. Documented exit codes and arguments stay compatible.

2
00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:18.216
Raj: We'll dry-run it first against fixed fixtures. Then compare isolated execution with the old artifact.

3
00:00:18.216 --> 00:00:25.967
Lukas: Keep volatile timestamps normalized in comparison. Don't mask meaningful differences such as row ordering.

4
00:00:25.967 --> 00:00:33.911
Priya: Just to confirm, the vertical slice needs review, right? Passing tests alone won't approve production.

5
00:00:33.911 --> 00:00:42.791
Anika: Yes, I'll sign off consumer output compatibility. Maybe weekly report fixtures need separate acceptance later.

6
00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:51.839
Hannah: The smoke test must include missing configuration. It should fail safely without partial published reports.

7
00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:58.631
Lukas: A mismatch is our future rollback trigger. Stop the new job before restoring old scheduling.

8
00:00:58.631 --> 00:01:06.382
Raj: Okay, no overlapping writers during any switch. I'll retain the old artifact and configuration.

9
00:01:06.382 --> 00:01:12.982
Priya: Let's record those gates in the plan. Mid-iteration review will check evidence against them.

10
00:01:12.982 --> 00:01:19.990
Anika: Agreed, the plan is ready to start. We'll reconvene next Wednesday with actual progress.

